        "tag": "title",
        "text": "92"
      },
      {
        "y": 23.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 478,
        "tag": "title",
        "text": "Collocation: which words go together"
      },
      {
        "y": 70.5,
        "x0": 75.1,
        "x1": 260,
        "tag": "title",
        "text": "A Adjective + noun collocations"
      },
      {
        "y": 88.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 441.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Nouns often have typical adjectives which go with them. Here are some examples."
      },
      {
        "y": 104.3,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 214.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Compare thing and article:"
      },
      {
        "y": 122.7,
        "x0": 105.1,
        "x1": 295.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "we say we don’t usually say"
      },
      {
        "y": 136.9,
        "x0": 105.1,
        "x1": 283.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "the real thing the genuine thing"
      },
      {
        "y": 151.3,
        "x0": 105.1,
        "x1": 271.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "the genuine article the real article"
      },
      {
        "y": 171.3,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 498.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "I don’t like five-a-side football; I prefer the real thing. [i.e. real football, with 11 players in each team]"
      },
      {
        "y": 183.3,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 450.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "These trainers are the genuine article. Those others are just cheap imported copies."
      },
      {
        "y": 199.6,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 388.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "You can give a broad summary of something (NOT a wide summary)."
      },
      {
        "y": 211.6,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 360,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "You can describe something in great detail (NOT in big detail)."
      },
      {
        "y": 228.2,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 373.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Some adjectives go with a restricted range of nouns. For example:"
      },
      {
        "y": 239.8,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 319.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "a formidable opponent/reputation/task/challenge"
      },
      {
        "y": 261.2,
        "x0": 74.7,
        "x1": 244.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "B Verb + adverb collocations"
      },
      {
        "y": 283.3,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 509.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Often, verbs have typical adverbs that collocate with them. The lines here show which collocations"
      },
      {
        "y": 295.3,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 147.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "are normal:"
      },
      {
        "y": 312.6,
        "x0": 109.1,
        "x1": 302.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "She always walks too fast."
      },
      {
        "y": 330.3,
        "x0": 283.5,
        "x1": 318.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "quickly."
      },
      {
        "y": 347.9,
        "x0": 109.1,
        "x1": 400.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Let’s move swiftly on to the next point."
      },
      {
        "y": 369.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 372.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "It’s something I feel strongly about (NOT I feel powerfully about)."
      },
      {
        "y": 381.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 428.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "If I remember rightly, it happened at about 6.30 (NOT If I remember perfectly)."
      },
      {
        "y": 403.2,
        "x0": 75,
        "x1": 270.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "C Adverb + adjective collocations"
      },
      {
        "y": 421.1,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 512.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "It is useful to learn which adverbs most typically modify particular types of adjectives. For example,"
      },
      {
        "y": 432.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 514.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "the adverb utterly, which means totally or completely, very frequently occurs before adjectives with"
      },
      {
        "y": 445.1,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 517.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "negative connotations, although it can also be used with neutral or positive words. Typical examples"
      },
      {
        "y": 456.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 514.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "are: appalling, dismal, depressed, disgusting, distasteful, exhausted, false, fatuous, impossible,"
      },
      {
        "y": 468.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 513.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "lost, ludicrous, naive, pointless, ridiculous, unacceptable, useless, wrong. Try to notice this kind"
      },
      {
        "y": 481.1,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 242.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "of regularity when learning words."
      },
      {
        "y": 502,
        "x0": 74.4,
        "x1": 240.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "D Verb + object collocations"
      },
      {
        "y": 519.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 296.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Verbs and their objects often form collocations."
      },
      {
        "y": 531.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 345.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "You raise your hand to ask a question (NOT lift your hand)."
      },
      {
        "y": 543.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 342.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "You can raise a family. [bring up children] (NOT lift a family)"
      },
      {
        "y": 555.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 322.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "You can visit / go to / click on / check out a website."
      },
      {
        "y": 579.5,
        "x0": 110.7,
        "x1": 205,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Language help"
      },
      {
        "y": 603.4,
        "x0": 111.7,
        "x1": 493.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Collocation is concerned with the way words regularly occur together, often in unpredictable ways."
      },
      {
        "y": 615.8,
        "x0": 111.7,
        "x1": 489.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "It is a very good idea when learning new words to learn any typical collocations that go with them."
      }
    ],
